From: grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: mediatek: initialize and calibrate AN7581 GSW PHYs

mt7988_setup() asserts SYS_CTRL_PHY_RST before mt7530_setup_mdio(),
resetting the four AN7581 internal GSW PHYs (MDIO 9..12) to silicon
defaults with BMCR_PDOWN set and wiping bootloader calibration.

Join MDIO 9..12 as a PHY package in an7581_phy_probe(), load the stock
eth_ephy Clause-45, Clause-22, and Token-Ring baseline tables across
the package once, run shared Rext calibration on MDIO 9 followed by
per-port R45, TX offset, and TX amplitude calibration with per-port TX
amplitude compensation, apply the runtime DSP/Token-Ring registers with
EEE advertisement cleared and downshift enabled, and clear BMCR_PDOWN
for enabled ports in an7581_phy_config_init(). Keep a separate
an7583_phy_probe() so AN7583 stays unchanged.

Signed-off-by: grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
